# Deny-by-default Docker build context (audit F22).
#
# Dockerfile.verifier is built from the repo root, so without this file the
# ENTIRE repo — including gitignored key material such as
# deployer-testnet.key.json (plaintext testnet owner/treasury/resolver key) —
# is shipped to the Docker daemon as build context. Exclude everything, then
# re-include exactly what Dockerfile.verifier COPYs.
*

# Dockerfile.verifier COPY sources: `COPY src ...` and `COPY problems/${PROBLEM} ...`.
!src
!problems
!schemas
!requirements.runtime.lock

# The Dockerfile itself (the classic builder reads it from the context;
# BuildKit sends it out-of-band, so this is harmless there).
!Dockerfile.verifier

# Belt-and-braces: never ship key material or env files even if one ever
# lands inside a re-included tree above.
**/*.key.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem

# Python build junk: nondeterministic bytes that would bloat the image and
# perturb the verifier-image hash.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
